From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: xfrm: dispatch only EIP-owned states to EIP

Do not replace the per-family output function from a loadable provider.  It
is shared by ESP, AH and IPComp and is copied into long-lived dst bundles,
which lets non-EIP bundles retain a stale module function after unload.
Dispatch through the EIP state type only when that state was successfully
claimed; native and unsupported states continue through the normal path.

Allocate an XFRM security context before provider initialization so a
provider can reject labelled states instead of claiming them before their
label is visible.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/xfrm/xfrm_output.c
+++ b/net/xfrm/xfrm_output.c
@@ -784,6 +784,8 @@ int xfrm_output(struct sock *sk, struct s
 	}
 
 	secpath_reset(skb);
+	if (unlikely(x->xflags & XFRM_STATE_OFFLOAD_EIP))
+		return x->type->output(x, skb);
 
 	if (xfrm_dev_offload_ok(skb, x)) {
 		struct sec_path *sp;
--- a/net/xfrm/xfrm_user.c
+++ b/net/xfrm/xfrm_user.c
@@ -973,11 +973,6 @@ static struct xfrm_state *xfrm_state_cons
 	if (attrs[XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV])
 		x->xflags |= XFRM_STATE_OFFLOAD_DEV_REQUESTED;
 
-	/* State providers need the imported replay and lifetime state at init. */
-	err = __xfrm_init_state(x, extack);
-	if (err)
-		goto error;
-
 	if (attrs[XFRMA_SEC_CTX]) {
 		err = security_xfrm_state_alloc(x,
 						nla_data(attrs[XFRMA_SEC_CTX]));
@@ -985,6 +980,11 @@ static struct xfrm_state *xfrm_state_cons
 			goto error;
 	}
 
+	/* State providers need the imported replay and lifetime state at init. */
+	err = __xfrm_init_state(x, extack);
+	if (err)
+		goto error;
+
 	xfrm_set_type_offload(x, attrs[XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV]);
 	/* configure the hardware if offload is requested */
 	if (attrs[XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV]) {
-- 
